          <h2 id="sec2">2. Formal Mathematical Foundations (Verified in Lean 4)</h2>
          <p>
            All core isolation, memory, roofline, and multi-GPU pipeline properties are formally proved in pure <strong>Lean 4</strong> (<code>Init</code> core, zero external Mathlib dependencies, zero <code>sorry</code>) and cross-verified symbolically in SymPy.
          </p>

          <div class="paper-theorem">
            <p><strong>Theorem 1 (Exact Block-Diagonal Gradient Isolation &amp; Non-Zero Forward Modulation).</strong> <em>Consider M &ge; 2 post-bifurcation streams with disjoint parameter blocks &theta; = (&theta;<sup>(1)</sup>, &hellip;, &theta;<sup>(M)</sup>) and block transition h<sub>k</sub><sup>(i)</sup> = F<sub>k</sub><sup>(i)</sup>(h<sub>k&minus;1</sub><sup>(i)</sup>, &theta;<sub>k</sub><sup>(i)</sup>, &#123;sg(h<sub>k&minus;1</sub><sup>(r)</sup>)&#125;<sub>r&ne;i</sub>), where sg(x) = x forward and &part;sg(x)/&part;u = 0 backward. Then for all i &ne; j and every block k:</em></p>
            <div class="paper-equation">&part;L<sub>k</sub><sup>(i)</sup> / &part;&theta;<sup>(j)</sup> &equiv; 0, &emsp; &lang;g<sup>(i)</sup>, g<sup>(j)</sup>&rang; &equiv; 0, &emsp; I(H<sub>k</sub><sup>(i)</sup> ; H<sub>k&minus;1</sub><sup>(j)</sup> | H<sub>k&minus;1</sub><sup>(i)</sup>, &theta;<sub>k</sub><sup>(i)</sup>) &gt; 0 &emsp; (1)</div>
            <p><em>eliminating destructive cross-stream gradient conflict (&lang;g<sup>(i)</sup>, g<sup>(j)</sup>&rang; &lt; 0) while preserving non-zero forward cross-stream contextual modulation.</em></p>
          </div>

          <div class="paper-theorem">
            <p><strong>Theorem 2 (Peak Activation Memory O(L/K) &amp; Iso-Width Roofline Speedup Law).</strong> <em>(2A) Partitioning an L-layer network into K &ge; 2 eager local-plasticity blocks with immediate graph release yields M<sub>local</sub>(L, K) = (1/K) M<sub>global</sub>(L) + M<sub>aux</sub> &lt; M<sub>global</sub>(L) if and only if M<sub>aux</sub> &lt; ((K&minus;1)/K) M<sub>global</sub>(L). (2B) Packing total width C = M &middot; D into M &ge; 2 dense <code>torch.bmm</code> streams <a href="#ref13">[13]</a> over BN tokens with b-byte elements satisfies:</em></p>
            <div class="paper-equation">FLOPs<sub>par</sub> = (1 / M) FLOPs<sub>hom</sub>, &emsp; Bytes<sub>par</sub> &lt; Bytes<sub>hom</sub> &emsp; (2)</div>
            <p><em>On a GPU with ridge point R<sub>GPU</sub> = &Pi;<sub>peak</sub> / &beta;<sub>mem</sub>, whenever 2BND &ge; b R<sub>GPU</sub>(2BN + D), both kernels are compute-bound and strict wall-clock speedup T<sub>par</sub> + T<sub>ovh</sub> &lt; T<sub>hom</sub> holds iff T<sub>ovh</sub> &lt; ((M&minus;1)/M) T<sub>hom</sub>.</em></p>
          </div>

          <div class="paper-theorem">
            <p><strong>Theorem 3 (Zero-Bubble Asynchronous Local Pipeline Dominance).</strong> <em>Across P &ge; 2 GPUs and m &ge; 1 microbatches, backward-locked GPipe <a href="#ref6">[6]</a> achieves utilization U<sub>GPipe</sub>(P, m) = m / (P &minus; 1 + m). Removing cross-stage backward dependencies via local plasticity <a href="#ref5">[5]</a> eliminates pipeline bubbles, yielding steady-state utilization U<sub>local</sub>(&epsilon;<sub>comm</sub>) = 1 / (1 + &epsilon;<sub>comm</sub>), which strictly exceeds GPipe iff &epsilon;<sub>comm</sub> &lt; (P &minus; 1) / m.</em></p>
          </div>

          <h2 id="sec3">3. SPRINT-LP v5: GPU-Native &amp; Bio-Faithful Unified Architecture</h2>
          <p>To bridge hardware speed and natural-image representation quality, <strong>SPRINT-LP v5</strong> combines four systems and neuro-inspired primitives (Figure 1):</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Pure Tensor-Core Stream Packing (<code>torch.baddbmm</code>):</strong> Replaces slow <code>Conv2d(groups=M)</code> kernels with contiguous batched GEMMs (<code>cublasGemmStridedBatchedEx</code>) <a href="#ref11">[11]</a> over <code>[M, B&middot;N, d]</code> tensors aligned to multiples of 8/64.</li>
            <li><strong>Whole-Step <code>torch.cuda.CUDAGraph</code> + Static FP16 + Fused AdamW:</strong> Captures all <code>K</code> local blocks' forward, loss, backward, <code>_foreach_mul_</code> static descaling (<code>S = 256.0</code>), gradient clipping, and fused capturable AdamW <a href="#ref14">[14]</a> <a href="#ref15">[15]</a> into a single CPU launch (~30 &mu;s), eliminating 4&times; dynamic <code>GradScaler</code> host-device syncs.</li>
            <li><strong>Bio-Faithful Shared V1/V2 Stem + Late Bifurcation:</strong> Stage 1 (<code>16&times;16, C = 96</code>) uses dense <code>groups=1</code> convolutions to capture synergistic early edges without &radic;M bandwidth inflation, before bifurcating at Stage 2 (<code>8&times;8</code>) and Stage 3 (<code>4&times;4</code>) into hard-isolated Ventral/Dorsal <code>torch.baddbmm</code> streams coupled by stop-gradient <strong>CG-LatFiLM</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>2-Unit Deep-MAN++ Anti-Myopia + Zero-Bubble T4&times;2 Pipeline:</strong> Each early block trains through a gradient-free EMA shadow (<code>&alpha; = 0.995</code>, updated via <code>_foreach_lerp_</code>) of the full downstream block <a href="#ref8">[8]</a> paired with detached <em>Shared-Output Readout</em> <a href="#ref9">[9]</a>. On 2 GPUs, GPU 0 (Blocks 1&ndash;2) and GPU 1 (Block 3) run 100% concurrently via ping-pong double buffers and non-blocking CUDA events.</li>
          </ol>

