          <h2 id="sec4">4. Empirical Validation &amp; Counterfactual Falsification on Kaggle T4&times;2</h2>

          <h3 id="sec4-1">4.1 Single-GPU Bonus Discovery: L2 Cache Locality Beats Global BP at 100% Identical Parameters</h3>
          <p>
            Evaluating Part I-B (<code>L = 12</code> <code>PureBMMStreamBlock</code> layers, <code>M = 3, d = 128</code>, <strong>100% identical model and parameter count</strong> on a single T4), partitioning from <code>K = 1</code> (Global BP) to <code>K = 6</code> (Local BP) not only follows Theorem 2A by cutting peak activation VRAM by <strong>79.0%</strong> (<code>758.1 &rarr; 159.2 MB</code>), but also <strong>monotonically accelerates wall-clock speed by 11.5%</strong> (<code>54.71 &rarr; 48.43 ms/step</code>; Table 2). Because <code>K = 6</code> executes backward immediately after 2 layers, intermediate activations remain hot in the T4's 4 MB L2 cache instead of spilling to 320 GB/s GDDR6 as in <code>K = 1</code>.
          </p>

