          <h3 id="sec4-2">4.2 Counterfactual Falsification Matrix (CF-1 through CF-4)</h3>
          <p>To prove strict causality rather than coincidence, we deliberately broke each theorem's governing mechanism on live T4&times;2 hardware (Figure 2):</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>CF-1 (Break Theorem 1):</strong> With <code>.detach()</code> on <code>CG-LatFiLM</code>, gradient leakage from Stream 0's loss into Stream 1's weights is exact <code>0.00000000</code>. Removing <code>.detach()</code> immediately causes non-zero gradient leakage (<code>2.02 &times; 10<sup>&minus;9</sup> &gt; 0</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>CF-2 (Break Theorem 2A):</strong> Removing <code>.detach()</code> at block boundaries on <code>K = 4</code> causes peak activation VRAM to rebound <strong>3.45&times;</strong> (<code>219.6 &rarr; 758.1 MB</code>, returning identically to <code>K = 1</code> Global BP).</li>
            <li><strong>CF-3 (Break Theorem 3 on T4&times;2):</strong> Re-introducing synchronous backward-locked pipeline bubbles degrades 2-GPU latency from <strong><code>16.96 ms</code></strong> to <strong><code>41.82 ms</code></strong> (confirming a <strong><code>2.47&times;</code></strong> real 2-GPU speedup on identical parameters).</li>
            <li><strong>CF-4 (Break Anti-Myopia):</strong> Removing Deep-MAN++ EMA shadows drops <code>AffCIFAR-10</code> Pose R<sup>2</sup> (<code>+0.325 &rarr; +0.308</code>) and class accuracy (<code>77.58% &rarr; 77.08%</code>).</li>
          </ul>

